/-!
# (key: carrier-check) Bridged word B_2 with the carrier certificate `Cr2h16`, h = 16: from the network certificate to the theorems

GENERATED by checks/wht12/carrier-check/py/crate.py (theorem texts of checks/wht9/bridge-rate/py/b2inst.py).  No `sorry`.

One unit: `W = 9362` live roles (`4 * cert.v + cert.R`: four bank roles for each of the `v = 560` classes,
`R = 7122` helper slots), label dimension `m = 80`, deficit `D = 1035`.
`unitPrice φ = 5 * rcost φ cert.invRanks + v * bankPrice h φ` = the price of `BlockAccounting.blocksB2Ke16` (`unit_cost`,
through the kernel-counted `CarrierCr2h16.ranks_cost`).
Whole-block `1 - 53992/10^8` (fails at 53993), ten decimals `1 - 5399225/10^10` (fails at 5399227);
per-rank `1 - 31553/10^8` (fails at 31558), ten decimals `1 - 3155781/10^10` (fails at 3155783).
NOTHING here constructs the network: the hypothesis `h : BCert α e c` is supplied in `Work.CarrierCheck.B2Ke16`.
-/

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

namespace OAI
